## Data Model

```
Project
├── id            (UUID)
├── name          (string)        — e.g. "Search Redesign", "Payments V2"
├── description   (text, optional)
├── status        (active | archived)
├── created_at    (timestamp)
├── updated_at    (timestamp)
│
└── Tasks[]
    ├── id            (UUID)
    ├── project_id    (FK → Project)
    ├── title         (string)
    ├── description   (text, optional)
    ├── status        (todo | in_progress | done)
    ├── priority      (low | medium | high | urgent)
    ├── due_date      (date, optional)
    ├── source        (manual | slack)
    ├── slack_raw     (text, optional)  — original Slack message text
    ├── created_at    (timestamp)
    └── updated_at    (timestamp)
```

---

## API Reference

### Projects

| Method | Path                  | Description            |
|--------|-----------------------|------------------------|
| GET    | /api/projects         | List all projects      |
| POST   | /api/projects         | Create a project       |
| GET    | /api/projects/:id     | Get project detail     |
| PUT    | /api/projects/:id     | Update a project       |
| DELETE | /api/projects/:id     | Archive a project      |

### Tasks

| Method | Path                                     | Description        |
|--------|------------------------------------------|--------------------|
| GET    | /api/projects/:id/tasks                  | List tasks          |
| POST   | /api/projects/:id/tasks                  | Create a task       |
| GET    | /api/projects/:id/tasks/:taskId          | Get task detail     |
| PUT    | /api/projects/:id/tasks/:taskId          | Update a task       |
| DELETE | /api/projects/:id/tasks/:taskId          | Delete a task       |
| PATCH  | /api/projects/:id/tasks/:taskId/status   | Quick status update |

### Dashboard

| Method | Path            | Description                         |
|--------|-----------------|-------------------------------------|
| GET    | /api/dashboard  | Aggregated stats across all projects|

---

## Slack Paste-to-Task

Quickly turn Slack messages into tracked tasks without any API setup:

1. **Copy** a message in Slack (Slack formats it as `[timestamp] Author: message`)
2. **Click** "New Task from Slack" on any project
3. **Paste** the Slack content into the modal
4. The app **parses** the paste and pre-fills:
   - Author → description ("Reported by: ...")
   - Message body → task title + description
   - Raw text → stored for reference
5. **Edit** the pre-filled fields if needed, then save

Tasks created this way are tagged with `source: slack` and retain the original
Slack text in the `slack_raw` field.

